{
  "$comment": [
    "Every shadcn/ui component GUML has no builtin for, as a GUML vocabulary.",
    "",
    "The components in `src/components/ui/` are the real ones, installed with `shadcn add --all` \u2014 61",
    "files, 331 exports, on Radix/Base UI, cmdk, embla, recharts and the rest. They are not a",
    "reimplementation and are not meant to be edited here; `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <name>` updates",
    "one in place, which is shadcn's own model.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS AND IS NOT A TAG HERE, because the distinction is the whole design:",
    "",
    "  * A builtin already covers most of them. `card`, `btn`, `badge`, `input`, `select`, `table`,",
    "    `tabs`, `modal`, `drawer`, `sidebar`, `skeleton`, `progress`, `toast`, `avatar`, `breadcrumb`",
    "    and `pagination` are in the compiler's own vocabulary and already wear shadcn's classes through",
    "    the default *theme*. A package may not shadow a builtin (`GUML0092`), and a second spelling of",
    "    each would split every document's vocabulary in two for nothing.",
    "  * Composition helpers are not document concepts. `Field`, `Item`, `InputGroup`, `ButtonGroup`'s",
    "    internals, `Direction` \u2014 those arrange other components. GUML expresses arrangement with",
    "    `row`/`col`/`grid` and modifiers, so exposing them as tags would be two ways to say one thing.",
    "  * `chart`, `calendar`, `date`, `upload` and `command` belong to `@guml/widgets`, the worked",
    "    example in `spec/REGISTRY.md`. Two packages declaring one name cannot both load, so they are",
    "    left there and this package covers everything else.",
    "",
    "Every entry is `app` level and `needs_runtime`: these are React components with real behaviour, so",
    "the no-JavaScript backend reports them rather than emitting markup that silently does nothing."
  ],
